[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745312896","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104359#issuecomment-2745312896","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104359","id":2745312896,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6joiaA","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-22T15:07:17Z","updated_at":"2025-03-22T15:07:17Z","body":"In my opinion, sending NaNs to the physics engine should not be supported. NaNs spread like wildfire during the simulation step:\n\nForce NaN -> Velocity NaN\nVelocity NaN -> Velocity NaN of all touching bodies and bodies attached through constraints\nVelocity NaN -> Position NaN\nPosition NaN -> Bounding Box NaN\nBounding Box NaN -> Broad Phase Tree NaN\n\nA broad phase with NaN values (depending on the implementation) loses its ability to quickly filter out non-colliding body pairs. In the narrow phase (as can be seen in the callstack above) this can mean testing the NaN body against every triangle. \n\nWhen implementing Jolt, I tried to reduce the damage that NaNs cause as much as possible, but I was not willing to spend extra cycles doing `isnan` checks everywhere. So in a lot of cases the Jolt simulation is borked too. At best the body and all bodies that were in contact disappear as the position becomes NaN. Worst case the simulation grids to a halt as way too much collision detection is performed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745312896/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753417194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104359#issuecomment-2753417194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104359","id":2753417194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kHc_q","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T07:02:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T07:02:23Z","body":"Could testing for `NaN`s just once in `apply_central_force()` and similar functions could do the trick ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753417194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755716082","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104359#issuecomment-2755716082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104359","id":2755716082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kQOPy","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T20:49:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T20:49:37Z","body":"That would certainly fix it, but then the question is: why only on `apply_central_force`? To be consistent you would need to check every vector / matrix / quaternion / float that goes into the API for NaNs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755716082/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]